  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 3.1.1.1, 'Process matrix illustrating three example processes within a typical vaccination programme'. A table with the columns Process, Objective, Task set and Outcomes, holding four rows. A Patient management keeps a database of all newborns and their vaccination history (register, search, maintain), leading to more complete registration. B Vaccination management ensures every infant receives all scheduled doses (define the schedule, plan, send reminders, register vaccinations, monitor coverage), leading to more timely vaccination and higher coverage. C Stock management keeps vaccines available while minimizing wastage (order, receive, store, count, monitor balances and expiry), leading to higher availability and lower wastage. D Service delivery ensures quality vaccination services (counsel, diagnose, dispense, refer, update the record, schedule the next visit), leading to correct protocol, timelier vaccinations and better documentation.",
